  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🐾 Pet Sitting Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for pet sitters, cat sitters and house sitters, from Whiskers & Wags to Furry Godmother."
    },
    "intro": "Good pet sitting names feel warm and trustworthy, with a touch of fun: <em>Furry Godmother</em>, <em>Willowbrook Pet Minders</em> or <em>Auntie Sarah's Pet Care</em>. Owners hand a pet sitter their keys and their best friend, so the name should feel warm and trustworthy. This **Pet Sitting Name Generator** has names in seven styles, from catchy puns to professional names and ones built from your own name or town.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good pet sitting names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Furry Godmother</strong>: a pun owners remember, and it promises good care.</li><li><strong>Purr-sonal Assistants</strong>: funny, and it covers cats as well as dogs.</li><li><strong>Hairy Houseguests</strong>: for sitters who have pets to stay.</li><li><strong>Whiskers &amp; Wags</strong>: cats and dogs in one catchy pair.</li><li><strong>Snoozy Whiskers</strong>: cute and calm.</li><li><strong>Willowbrook Pet Minders</strong>: a classic, trustworthy name for regular clients.</li><li><strong>Roost</strong>: one modern word, with a sense of home.</li><li><strong>Auntie Sarah's Pet Care</strong>: your own name, with family warmth built in.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Sitting, minding or boarding?",
        "content": "<p>The words in the name tell owners what you offer before they ring.</p><ul><li><em>Pet sitting</em> usually means you look after pets in their own home, or pop in to feed them.</li><li><em>Pet minding</em> is the same idea, and a little more British.</li><li><em>Pet boarding</em> means the pets stay with you. In England that usually needs an animal activity licence from your council.</li><li><em>Pet care</em> covers all of these, plus walks, so it leaves room to grow.</li></ul><p>Cats, rabbits and birds are often looked after at home, so a name that isn't only about dogs (<em>Feathers &amp; Whiskers</em>, <em>The Cheeky Critters Club</em>) brings in more clients.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>Every name here has a <strong>Check</strong> button, which opens the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>: it looks up domains, social handles, the company register and trade mark searches in one place. Before you order signs or cards:</p><ul><li><strong>Company register.</strong> In the UK, search Companies House; a limited company's name can't be the same as one already registered. In the US, search your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Trade marks.</strong> Search the UK Intellectual Property Office or the USPTO for marks in your line of work. Registering a company doesn't give you trade mark rights.</li><li><strong>Domain and handles.</strong> Try the .co.uk or .com and the Instagram and Facebook names at the same time, and change the name slightly rather than settle for a messy handle.</li><li><strong>Local search.</strong> Look up the name with your town. Two similar businesses a few miles apart confuse customers and reviews.</li></ul><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For the full process, read <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p><p>For the rest of the pet trade, try the <a href=\"dog-walking-name-generator.html\">Dog Walking</a> and <a href=\"dog-grooming-name-generator.html\">Dog Grooming</a> name generators.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_care-names.html\">pet, care and learning business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good pet sitting business names?",
        "answer": "Warm, trustworthy names with a little fun, like Furry Godmother, Whiskers & Wags or Willowbrook Pet Minders. Your own name, as in Auntie Sarah's Pet Care, works well for a local sitter."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should I call it pet sitting, pet care or pet boarding?",
        "answer": "Pet sitting means you look after pets in their own home, or pop in to feed them. Pet boarding means the pets stay with you, which usually needs a licence (in England, an animal activity licence from your council). Pet care covers both, plus walks, so it leaves room to grow."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are funny pet sitting names?",
        "answer": "Puns that owners will repeat, like Furry Godmother, Purr-sonal Assistants or Hairy Houseguests. Choose the Funny style for more."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I check a pet sitting name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company name, a domain and a social media handle. Before you commit, search the official registers too: in the UK, Companies House; in the US, your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search."
      }
    ]
